Package: fastIWTlm
Type: Package
Title: Fast Interval-Wise Testing for Functional Linear Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Matteo", "Fontana", email = "mtt.fnt@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Alessia", "Pini", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           comment = "R code from which 'fastIWTlm()' is adapted"),
    person("Simone", "Vantini", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           comment = "co-author of the 'fdatest' code that code builds on"),
    person("Aymeric", "Stamm", role = "ctb",
           comment = "maintainer of 'fdatest'"))
Description: Interval-wise testing (Pini and Vantini (2017)
    <doi:10.1080/10485252.2017.1306627>; Abramowicz et al. (2018)
    <doi:10.1111/sjos.12333>) for linear models with a functional response
    and scalar or functional (concurrent) covariates. 'fastIWTlm()' gives
    the global F test and the partial t tests as functions over the domain,
    with p-values adjusted to control the interval-wise error rate. Its
    permutation loop can run in a parallel 'RcppEigen' kernel. Results can
    be summarised and plotted with 'ggplot2'.
